Maarten Hilhorst wrote:
> For the second time this game, I stumbled into a polymorph trap and
> changed into something big, and for the second time I lost my dwarvish
> scale mail and my robe. 
> 
> It's a bit frustrating, so I'd like to know what you do to prevent this
> kind of disaster. s move s move s move? Shout at the RNG? Any help would
> be much appreciated.
> 
> (I'm a lvl 14 archaeologist, so I've got searching. )

You cannot prevent that, you either need magic resistance, or a ring of
polymorph control, or an amulet of unchanging. Searching is very helpful
to reduce the risk. Further reduction is possible if you make use of lamps
to avoid searching too many squares in unlit rooms. Polymorph traps will
not be generated above dungeon level 8 so you may usually reach minetown
to get a light source from there. Taming as many monsters as possible will
make your pets guinea-pigs for an extended search. Once you've reached
dungeon level 8 you may switch from your precious armor to some redundant,
say some elven cloak, and just put it on again if you got MR or in cases
where you need to make use of your robe.

